- `canonSpace`, `canonConsistent`, `programv_of_canon`; extraction lemmas;
- `check_transfer`; `pol_low/pol_high`, `LowIface/HighIface`, `subT_iface_low/high` (LowIface <= any same-head iface target; any same-head iface <= HighIface);
- `convert_eqS_self`, `utsutbst`, `AssignRel`+`tsubst_sim`, `AssignRel_refl`, `check_context_lower`;
- **mutual representation relation** (Section MutRepSection): `RArgs i a b` (pointwise `RRep (a p) (b p)`) mutually with `RRep t u` with constructors `rrep_any` (any t represented by utanyT), `rrep_bot` (unreachable t by utbotT), `rrep_iface` (t <= stinterface i a and RArgs a b gives RRep t (utifaceT i b));
- `RRep_lower` (downward closed along S subtyping);
- `RRep_subst`: pointwise `RRep (sigma q) (tau q)` implies `RRep (tsubst sigma R) (utsubst tau R)` for any UserType R (uses mkRArgs and sstrefl);
- `RRep_obj`: given `SubSpace (stinterface j args) (stinterface i a)` and `RArgs i a b`, there exist canonical args c with `RArgs j args c` and `SubT (utifaceT j c) (utifaceT i b)`. Construction: consistency via ctsinterface gives j=i and pointwise signed S relations between args and a; set c p = b p for positive-variance p, c p = utanyT for negative; positive case uses RRep_lower, negative uses rrep_any; conclusion by subT_variance with refl/any.

Remaining core: the main expression simulation
  `RRep t u -> (context invariant) -> CheckExpression S ctx e t -> CheckExpression canon ctxc e u`.
`cesub` is handled by RRep_lower; `ceobject` uses RRep_obj + RRep_subst for bodies; `ceinvoke` uses RRep_obj-style argument choices and RRep for receiver/args. The hard remaining part is the context invariant at `ceinput`: canonical context entries must be below every target u with RRep (S entry) u. For formal inputs the canonical entry is `signatures_c.input`; for utany formals it must be utanyT (only rep of stany), for iface formals use RRep_obj's c, for variable formals the choice c p = b p (positive) / any (negative); conflicting variable uses at two interface heads are ruled out by S-consistency/ctsinterface (transitivity forces the same head when the target rep is an iface; if the target rep is any, an iface use would imply stany <= iface, contradiction). Formalizing this case analysis, then the canonical-check decider (bounded assignment search using Finite IParameter/Interface), remains.

Note: the global `Set Uniform Inductive Parameters` in Task.v affects new mutual inductives: recursive occurrences omit uniform parameters, constructors take parameters explicitly.

