Task.v: ~2445 lines; `make` fails only at `programv_decider` ("pending proofs"); no escapes. Verified additions (all in Task.v):
- enumeration/deciders: `dec_hierarchyv`, `dec_subT`, `dec_subuser`, `dec_signed_subuser`, `dec_unreachable_usertype`;
- canonical space: `canonSpace`, `canonConsistent`, `programv_of_canon`;
- extraction lemmas (`check_eobject_conformance`, `check_eobject_type`, `check_invoke_recv_method`, `top_eobject_head`, `check_einput_le`, `check_einvoke_decomp`);
- `check_transfer` (space-homomorphism transport);
- extremal argument types: `pol_low/pol_high`, `LowIface/HighIface`, `subT_iface_low/high` (`LowIface i <= any same-head b` for arbitrary b; `any same-head a <= HighIface i`);
- `convert_eqS_self` (convert along any eqS a a is identity, via UIP_dec);
- `utsutbst` (canonical UserType substitution), `AssignRel` (signed recursive assignment relation), `tsubst_sim` (if AssignRel holds and `Signed S.SubSpace s (tsubst sigma u) (tsubst sigma' u)`, then `Signed SubT s (utsubst tau u) (utsubst tau' u)`; interface case uses `ctsinterface` decomposition and convert_eqS_self);
- `AssignRel_refl` (AssignRel u s sigma sigma tau tau always holds);
- `check_context_lower` (CheckExpression monotone under lowering context entry types: ctx' entry <= ctx entry pointwise implies CheckExpression at ctx' too).

Key remaining core (isolated): the canonical **small-model / assignment representation lemma**. For a body of an object, `check_context_lower` lets one lower the S context from the actual signature inputs to the formal substituted inputs (formal <= actual) and widen the result, so S bodies may be assumed checked at formal substituted types `tsubst sigma R` with context formal substituted inputs (same assignment sigma). Choosing canonical `signatures := bssubst tau formal`, the canonical bodies must check at `utsubst tau R` with the same syntactic R. Needed: a two-type substitution simulation
  `Signed S.SubSpace s (tsubst sigma R1) (tsubst sigma R2) -> Signed SubT s (utsubst tau R1) (utsubst tau R2)`
under an assignment representation relation `TauRep sigma tau`. Variable cases need per-parameter canonical values chosen from {bot, any, LowIface/HighIface heads} so that all S constraints map to UT constraints; S-consistency (ctsanyinterface/ctsinterfaceunreachable) rules out conflicting demands (e.g. `stany <= sigma p <= iface`). Since IParameter/Interface are Finite, the canonical assignment can be assembled inside the SProp goal by enumerating parameters (SProp elimination into an SProp goal may use Type-valued extracted witnesses). This small-model lemma is the paper's core and the blocker.

